### VS Code REST Client console for the HTTP API
###
### Requires the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), which is in
### .vscode/extensions.json. Click "Send Request" above any request to run it;
### the response opens in a side panel.
###
### Setup:
###   1. Start the server:  Tasks -> "server: dev (autoreload)"
###   2. Mint a key:        Tasks -> "maintenance: mint API key"
###   3. Paste it below. The plaintext is shown once and stored only as a hash.
###
### Requests reference earlier responses by name (see @name upload), so the
### download and image links are picked up automatically -- no copy-pasting
### signed URLs, which is the point of using this over curl.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@apiKey = sk_PASTE_YOUR_KEY_HERE

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Liveness -- process is up
GET {{base}}/healthz

### Readiness -- storage is writable (this is the one to probe in production)
GET {{base}}/readyz

### OpenAPI document
GET {{base}}/openapi.json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth boundary -- all three should be 401
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### No credentials at all
POST {{base}}/api/v1/files
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="probe.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./scratch/notes.txt
------Boundary--

### A key that does not exist
POST {{base}}/api/v1/files
Authorization: Bearer sk_not-a-real-key
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="probe.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./scratch/notes.txt
------Boundary--

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Upload
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

# @name upload
POST {{base}}/api/v1/files
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="photo.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./scratch/photo.png
------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="ttl"

300
------Boundary--

### A non-image: no image_url is produced, mime falls back to octet-stream
POST {{base}}/api/v1/files
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./scratch/notes.txt
------Boundary--

### Malware gate -- requires the server started with AV_BACKEND=stub.
### Expect 201 with scan_status=infected and servable=false.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/files
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="payload.bin"
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ./scratch/evil.bin
------Boundary--

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Signed links -- the security core
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 200: the signed download link works
GET {{upload.response.body.$.download_url}}

### 200: the image display link, permanently public and unguessable
GET {{upload.response.body.$.image_url}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Tampering -- every one of these must be refused
###
### The signature is not exposed as a separate field (it only ever appears
### inside the signed URL), and REST Client cannot split a string out of a
### response, so these use bogus credentials rather than a reused-valid-sig
### variant. They still exercise the whole rejection path.
###
### For the sharper case -- a *valid* signature presented with a rewritten
### purpose -- copy the `sig=` value out of the upload response above and
### paste it below. That is the attack purpose-binding exists to stop.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 403: garbage signature with a plausible exp
GET {{base}}/d/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}?exp=9999999999&p=dl&sig=deadbeef

### 403: p=img with a signature that was minted for p=dl.
### PASTE_SIG must be replaced with the sig= value from the upload response;
### leaving it as-is still returns 403, just for the wrong reason.
GET {{base}}/d/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}?exp=9999999999&p=img&sig=PASTE_SIG

### 410: exp rewritten into the past.
### Expiry is checked before the signature, so this is Gone rather than
### Forbidden regardless of whether the MAC would have matched.
GET {{base}}/d/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}?exp=1&p=dl&sig=x

### 403: unknown file_id
GET {{base}}/d/NOTAREALID?exp=9999999999&p=dl&sig=deadbeef

### 404: image path whose sha8 does not match the record
GET {{base}}/i/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}/deadbeef.webp

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Metadata and links
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### File metadata, including width/height parsed server-side
GET {{base}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Markdown snippet ready to paste into a document
GET {{base}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Re-issue a link with a 60 second lifetime
POST {{base}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}/links
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ttl": 60,
  "purpose": "dl"
}

### Ask for an absurd TTL -- clamped to MAX_TTL (604800 by default)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}/links
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ttl": 99999999
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Listing, stats, deletion
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Recent uploads
GET {{base}}/api/v1/files?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Counts and disk pressure
GET {{base}}/api/v1/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Soft delete. The blob is reclaimed later by the cleanup sweep, because
### other records may reference the same content.
DELETE {{base}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### 404: the metadata is gone
GET {{base}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.file_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### 404: and so is the signed download link
GET {{upload.response.body.$.download_url}}
